# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and in the working tree
# on every platform, Windows included.
#
# This is not cosmetic. scripts/gen-migrations.mjs embeds the bytes of the
# db/*.sql files verbatim into src/lib/events/migrations.generated.ts, which is
# tracked. With core.autocrlf=true and no rules here, Windows checks the .sql
# files out as CRLF, the generator emits \r\n where macOS emitted \n, and the
# generated file shows as modified immediately after every build.
#
# The consequence is worse than a noisy diff: scripts/update.mjs refuses to pull
# into a dirty tree by design, so on a Windows box the self-updater silently
# stops updating after the first build and only says so in a log line.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the files that feed the generator.
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

# PowerShell is happy with LF, and keeping it uniform means a script authored on
# macOS is byte-identical on the deployment box.
*.ps1   text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary